@page "/"
@inject BrowserStorage Storage
<PageTitle>NServiceBus Wizard</PageTitle>

@* Each paragraph is one source line: a line break inside text survives into the rendered markup as a run of spaces. *@
<p>Pick a starting point. Each flow asks a few questions, then produces a guide, a download and markdown for an AI assistant.</p>

<div class="entry-cards">
    <a class="entry-card" href="new">
        <h2>New endpoint</h2>
        <p>Start from scratch: hosting, transport, persistence, serializer and tests, plus any features. The result is a solution that builds and runs.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="entry-card" href="add">
        <h2>Add features to an existing endpoint</h2>
        <p>Pick features to add: sagas, the outbox, monitoring, or an NServiceBus Community extension. The result is only what has to be merged in.</p>
    </a>
</div>

<p class="hint">Every page's url holds the choices made so far, so any point can be bookmarked or shared.</p>
<p class="hint forget">This browser remembers the transport and the persistence of the endpoint features were last added to, to fill them in next time. <button type="button" class="link-button" @onclick="Forget">@forgetLabel</button></p>

@code {
    string forgetLabel = "Forget them";

    async Task Forget()
    {
        await Storage.ForgetAsync();
        forgetLabel = "Forgotten";
    }
}
